@startuml descriptor-doctrine-kinds
' Field-level schemas of the six doctrine descriptor kinds.
' Sources: src/charter/offering/schemas/{directive,tactic,paradigm,styleguide,toolguide,procedure}.schema.yaml
' Notation: + required, - optional. All top-level objects are additionalProperties:false.
' Decided design: ADR-0052 (procedures tightened, anti-patterns as authored artifacts), accepted 2026-11-02; not built yet.
'   Inline anti-patterns leave procedure and styleguide (d4, d16); guidance carries rejects (d9); AntiPattern is a file (d8).
' Pending: a yellow <<pending>> class or a [pending ADR-00xx OQn] suffix marks a part whose open question is not ruled.
!include _style.iuml
title Doctrine descriptor schemas — decided design (ADR-0052)

class Directive <<directive.schema.yaml>> {
  + id : string ~ ^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_-]*$
  + schema_version : "1.0"
  + title : string
  + intent : string
  + enforcement : Enforcement
  - scope : string
  - procedures : string[]
  - integrity_rules : string[]
  - validation_criteria : string[]
  - explicit_allowances : string[1..] [required if lenient-adherence]
  - references : Reference[]
  - rejects : RejectsRef[]
}
enum Enforcement {
  required
  lenient-adherence
  advisory
}
class Reference <<directive/paradigm/procedure_reference>> {
  + type : RefKind
  + id : string
  - when : string [directive only]
  - reason : string [directive, procedure]
}
enum RefKind {
  directive, tactic, styleguide, toolguide,
  paradigm, procedure, agent_profile,
  mission_step_contract, template
}

class RejectsRef <<rejects entry (ADR-0052 d9)>> {
  + type : anti_pattern
  + id : string
  + reason : string
}

class Tactic <<tactic.schema.yaml>> {
  + id : string ~ ^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$
  + schema_version : "1.0"
  + name : string
  + steps : TacticStep[1..]
  - purpose : string
  - failure_modes : string[]
  - applies_to_languages : string[]
  - references : TacticReference[1..]
  - rejects : RejectsRef[]
  - notes : string
}
class TacticStep {
  + title : string
  - description : string
  - examples : string[1..]
  - references : TacticReference[1..]
}
class TacticReference {
  + name : string
  + type : RefKind minus agent_profile, mission_step_contract
  + id : string
  + when : string
}

class Paradigm <<paradigm.schema.yaml>> {
  + schema_version : "1.0"
  + id : string ~ ^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$
  + name : string
  + summary : string
  - directive_refs : string[] ~ ^DIRECTIVE_\d{3}$
  - references : Reference[]
  - rejects : RejectsRef[]
}

class Toolguide <<toolguide.schema.yaml>> {
  + id : string ~ ^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$
  + schema_version : "1.0"
  + tool : string
  + title : string
  + guide_path : string ~ relative *.md
  + summary : string
  - commands : string[]
  - applies_to_languages : string[]
  - last_updated : string
  - references : string[]
}

class Procedure <<procedure.schema.yaml>> {
  + schema_version : "1.0"
  + id : string ~ ^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$
  + name : string
  + purpose : string
  + entry_condition : string
  + exit_condition : string
  + steps : ProcedureStep[1..]
  - applies_to_languages : string[]
  - notes : string
  - references : Reference[]
  - rejects : RejectsRef[]
}
class ProcedureStep {
  + title : string
  - description : string
  - actor : human | agent | system = agent
  - on_success : string
  - on_failure : string
}
note right of Procedure
  A repeatable, bounded episode used inside one step (ADR-0052 d2).
  It may not produce the Mission's deliverables, span steps or be a rule.
  The check is curation by review, not a schema refusal (d3).
  Inline anti_patterns are removed (d4, d16); use rejects.
end note

class Styleguide <<styleguide.schema.yaml>> {
  + id : string ~ ^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$
  + schema_version : "1.0"
  + title : string
  + scope : StyleScope
  + principles : string[1..]
  - patterns : Pattern[1..]
  - tooling : map<string,string>
  - quality_test : string
  - applies_to_languages : string[]
  - references : string[]
  - rejects : RejectsRef[]
  - structural_lint_config : StructuralLintConfig
}
enum StyleScope {
  code, docs, architecture,
  testing, operations, glossary
}
class Pattern {
  + name : string
  + description : string
  - bad_example : string
  - good_example : string
}
class AntiPattern <<pending>> <<anti-pattern.schema.yaml>> {
  + schema_version : "1.0"
  + id : string (kebab-case, the file stem)
  + title : string
  + description : string
  + severity : Severity <color:#8A6D00>[pending ADR-0052 OQ2]</color>
  - bad_example : string
  - good_example : string
  --
  file: anti_patterns/<id>.anti-pattern.yaml <color:#8A6D00>[pending ADR-0052 OQ2]</color>
  migrated entries default to smell <color:#8A6D00>[pending ADR-0052 OQ4]</color>
  a file-less anti_pattern node is refused <color:#8A6D00>[pending ADR-0052 OQ3]</color>
}
enum Severity {
  smell
  severe
  breaking
}
class StructuralLintConfig {
  - curated_complete_sections, point_in_time_patterns,
    point_in_time_markers, frontmatter_required_fields, ...
  [docs structural-lint options; all optional]
}

Directive --> Enforcement
Directive *-- "*" Reference
Paradigm *-- "*" Reference
Procedure *-- "*" Reference
Reference --> RefKind
Tactic *-- "1..*" TacticStep
Tactic *-- "*" TacticReference
TacticStep *-- "*" TacticReference
Procedure *-- "1..*" ProcedureStep
Styleguide --> StyleScope
Styleguide *-- "*" Pattern
Directive ..> RejectsRef
Tactic ..> RejectsRef
Paradigm ..> RejectsRef
Styleguide ..> RejectsRef
Procedure ..> RejectsRef
RejectsRef ..> AntiPattern : type + id
AntiPattern --> Severity
Styleguide *-- "0..1" StructuralLintConfig
note bottom of RejectsRef
  rejects sits beside references, same shape on every guidance kind (ADR-0052 d9).
  Toolguide and agent profiles carry none; mission types and their steps do
  (drawn in descriptor-mission-type-lifecycle).
  Directive, tactic, paradigm and styleguide mint Relation.rejects, never suggests;
  a procedure's entry is kept verbatim until #189 rules (d9).
  Glossary avoid is not an anti-pattern (d12).
end note
legend right
  + required, - optional.
  Yellow <<pending>> / [pending …]: decided in the cited ADR,
  but the cited open question is not ruled.
endlegend
@enduml
